  (text "R-LED-PD holds the input low through the bootloader window: GPIO1 floats, OE is tied low,\nand a floating AHCT input would put clean 5 V edges into the LED row before firmware runs.\nGates B-D are spare: inputs and enables tied low (an enabled CMOS gate never floats).\n\nTHE LED ROW (ADR 0028): 13 x WS2815B-V1 on the main board, 12 V, one data line.\nEach LED's DIN1 is the DO of the LED before it. Its DIN2, the backup input, is the DIN1 of the LED before it\n(the DO of the LED two back): if one LED dies, the next reads its data on DIN2 and the row keeps going.\nLED 1's DIN2 is grounded, as the WS2815 recommended circuit draws it (datasheets/led/WS2815.pdf p.4);\nthe WS2815B-V1 sheet draws no application circuit. LED 13's DO drives nothing.\n100 nF at every LED, VDD (pin 2) to GND (pin 5). Pin 1 is NC on the B-V1." (at 256.54 38.10 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid c7d8af21-9409-5396-b419-271cc4e3455a))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
